<a:ObjectID>D7B185EA-18DD-43A9-A9E7-44267FDFC8AB</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>QUALITY61850</a:Name>
<a:Code>QUALITY61850</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Quality flags in this class are as defined in IEC 61850, except for estimatorReplaced, which has been included in this class for convenience.</a:Comment>
<a:PhysicalOptions>pctfree 10
initrans 1
maxtrans 255
storage
(
    initial 64K
    minextents 1
    maxextents unlimited
)
tablespace IEC
logging
monitoring
 noparallel</a:PhysicalOptions>
<c:Columns>
<o:Column Id="o1597">
<a:ObjectID>A4925682-13A5-49CA-8642-DFB625CAE66B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>VALIDITY</a:Name>
<a:Code>VALIDITY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Validity may be good, questionable or invalid. Refer to the Validity enumeration for more details.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER</a:DataType>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1598">
<a:ObjectID>7A52FBA5-91A1-4730-98BF-8F83660786F9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OVERFLOW</a:Name>
<a:Code>OVERFLOW</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is beyond the capability of being  represented properly. For example, a counter value overflows from maximum count back to a value of zero.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1599">
<a:ObjectID>007590BE-69DA-4593-99D6-8283048FEAA6</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OUTOFRANGE</a:Name>
<a:Code>OUTOFRANGE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is beyond a predefined range of value.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1600">
<a:ObjectID>99563C69-4DCF-4F03-AD5A-A0AE1374C3D0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>BADREFERENCE</a:Name>
<a:Code>BADREFERENCE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value may be incorrect due to a reference being out of calibration.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1601">
<a:ObjectID>FE355808-354A-4541-B656-D4B2348112C4</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OSCILLATORY</a:Name>
<a:Code>OSCILLATORY</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>To prevent some overload of the communication it is sensible to detect and suppress oscillating (fast changing) binary inputs. If a signal changes in a defined time (tosc) twice in the same direction (from 0 to 1 or from 1 to 0) then oscillation is detected and the detail quality identifier &quot;oscillatory&quot; is set. If it is detected a configured numbers of transient changes could be passed by. In this time the validity status &quot;questionable&quot; is set. If after this defined numbers of changes the signal is still in the oscillating state the value shall be set either to the opposite state of the previous stable value or to a defined default value. In this case the validity status &quot;questionable&quot; is reset and &quot;invalid&quot; is set as long as the signal is oscillating. If it is configured such that no transient changes should be passed by then the validity status &quot;invalid&quot; is set immediately in addition to the detail quality identifier &quot;oscillatory&quot; (used for status information only).</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1602">
<a:ObjectID>11E2E9E9-2ED5-44D1-89DE-52D23E5C5CAE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>FAILURE</a:Name>
<a:Code>FAILURE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>This identifier indicates that a supervision function has detected an internal or external failure, e.g. communication failure.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1603">
<a:ObjectID>EEE26178-3C47-4DF8-8041-3404DB56F7D8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OLDDATA</a:Name>
<a:Code>OLDDATA</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is old and possibly invalid, as it has not been successfully updated during a specified time interval.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1604">
<a:ObjectID>81C7C539-5951-4669-A1FD-B42420EB56B8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SUSPECT</a:Name>
<a:Code>SUSPECT</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A correlation function has detected that the value is not consitent with other values. Typically set by a network State Estimator.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1605">
<a:ObjectID>59AD8037-DCEE-4FAD-BB8E-5C83D3167FD8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>TEST</a:Name>
<a:Code>TEST</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is transmitted for test purposes.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1606">
<a:ObjectID>455EC96A-76D6-43E9-B27C-97F94242A16D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OPERATORBLOCKED</a:Name>
<a:Code>OPERATORBLOCKED</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is blocked and hence unavailable for transmission.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1607">
<a:ObjectID>4A26BC2F-CCCB-4B60-88E9-553EE46195C0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SOURCE</a:Name>
<a:Code>SOURCE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Source gives information related to the origin of a value. The value may be acquired from the process, defaulted or substituted.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER</a:DataType>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1608">
<a:ObjectID>777934CD-B050-4919-AD8D-9E2E853843BD</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ESTIMATORREPLACED</a:Name>
<a:Code>ESTIMATORREPLACED</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Value has been replaced by State Estimator. estimatorReplaced is not an IEC61850 quality bit but has been put in this class for convenience.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER(1)</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1609">
