<o:Table Id="o878">
<a:ObjectID>32EAF1BE-C3E5-489B-9F6A-A20DBD6A315A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>STATICVARCOMPENSATOR</a:Name>
<a:Code>STATICVARCOMPENSATOR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A facility for providing variable and controllable shunt reactive power. The SVC typically consists of a stepdown transformer, filter, thyristor-controlled reactor, and thyristor-switched capacitor arms.

The SVC may operate in fixed MVar output mode or in voltage control mode.  When in voltage control mode, the output of the SVC will be proportional to the deviation of voltage at the controlled bus from the voltage setpoint.  The SVC characteristic slope defines the proportion.  If the voltage at the controlled bus is equal to the voltage setpoint, the SVC MVar output is zero.</a:Comment>
<a:PhysicalOptions>pctfree 10
initrans 1
maxtrans 255
storage
(
    initial 64K
    minextents 1
    maxextents unlimited
)
tablespace IEC
logging
monitoring
 noparallel</a:PhysicalOptions>
<c:Columns>
<o:Column Id="o1718">
<a:ObjectID>66371358-F579-4EE0-8DCE-82DE8A60CC63</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>CAPACITIVERATING</a:Name>
<a:Code>CAPACITIVERATING</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1201276008</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1201276008</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Maximum available capacitive reactive power</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>NUMBER</a:DataType>
<a:Mandatory>1</a:Mandatory>
</o:Column>
<o:Column Id="o1719">
<a:ObjectID>01945AE3-6D03-4426-9FEC-151D425C255C</a:ObjectID>
